Remember how it was in the days of Noah. It will be the same when the Son of Man comes.
In the days before the flood, people were eating and drinking. They were marrying. They were giving their daughters in marriage. They were doing all those things until the day that Noah entered into the ark.
They knew nothing about what would happen until the flood came and took them all. That is how it will be when the Son of Man comes.
Two men will be in the field. One will be taken, and the other will be left.
Two women will grind with a hand mill. One will be taken and the other will be left.
So remain on alert. For you do not know on which day your Lord will come.
You must understand something. Suppose the homeowner knew at what time of night the thief was coming. Then he would keep watch. He would not let his house be robbed.
Therefore, you must also be ready. For the Son of Man will come at an hour when you do not expect him.
Let us suppose a master puts one of his servants in charge of the other servants in his house. The servant's task is to give them their food at the proper time. The master wants a servant who is faithful and wise for this purpose.
It will be to the advantage of the servant that he be found by his master doing his work when the master returns.
Here is what I will tell you is true. The master will give that servant charge over all that he has.
"But let us suppose that the server is malicious. Let us suppose that he says to himself, 'My master stays away for a long time.'"
