On a Saturday, Jesus was walking with his disciples through the grain fields. The disciples began to break off heads of some of the grain.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look! It is against the law to do these things on the Sabbath. Why do your disciples do this?"
He answered, "Have you never read about what David did? He and his men were hungry. They needed food."
When Abiathar was the high priest, David went into the house of God and ate some of the holy bread. Only the priests were allowed to eat it. David also gave some of the bread to his men."
Then Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man. But man was not made for the Sabbath.
"So the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath."
Healing on Saturday
Jesus entered the synagogue on another occasion. There was a man there who was bent over and could not straighten up.
Some Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They were watching him closely. They wanted to see if he would heal the man on the Sabbath.
Jesus spoke to the man who had a withered and crooked hand. He said to him, "Stand in front of everyone."
